Article 1 (Scope of Authorization) The limit of amount authorized per agency or position under Article 6 (2) of the Act on Liability of Accounting Personnel (hereinafter referred to as the “Act”) shall be classified as follows: <Amended by Presidential Decree No. 28266, Sep. 5, 2017; Presidential Decree No. 29304, Nov. 27, 2018>
  1. Where an order for compensation for loss of or damage to a commodity is issued pursuant to Article 46 of the Commodity Management Act: 
    (a) Agencies the heads of which are public officials of Grade I (including public officials in special service or extraordinary civil service equivalent thereto) or members in general service, special service, or extraordinary civil service of the Senior Executive Service: Less than six million won per case;
    (b) Agencies the heads of which are public officials of Grade II or III (including public officials in special service or extraordinary civil service equivalent thereto) or members in general service, special service, or extraordinary civil service of the Senior Executive Service: Less than four million won per case;
    (c) Agencies the heads of which are public officials of Grade IV or V (including public officials in special service or extraordinary civil service equivalent thereto): Less than two million won per case;
  2. Where an order for compensation for loss of or damage to munitions is issued pursuant to Article 28 (2) of the Act on the Management of Military Supplies: 
    (a) Chiefs of Staff of each armed force: Less than 10 million won per case;
    (b) National defense agencies or military units the heads of which are general-level officers of at least the rank of lieutenant general: Less than eight million won per case;
    (c) National defense agencies or military units the heads of which are general-level officers of at least the rank of brigadier general: Less than six million won per case;
    (d) National defense agencies the heads of which are public officials of Grade I (including public officials in special service or extraordinary civil service equivalent thereto) or members in general service, special service, or extraordinary civil service of the Senior Executive Service: Less than six million won per case;
    (e) National defense agencies the heads of which are public officials of Grade II or III (including public officials in special service or extraordinary civil service equivalent thereto) or members in general service, special service, or extraordinary civil service of the Senior Executive Service: Less than four million won per case.

Article 2 (Criteria for Compensation) Where the heads of each agency, each armed force, national defense agencies, or military units intend to make a disposition of order for compensation within the limit of amount authorized pursuant to the subparagraphs of Article 1, they shall make such disposition according to the following criteria and report the results thereof to the competent Minister or the head of the pertinent supervisory agency without delay: <Amended by Presidential Decree No. 29304, Nov. 27, 2018>
  1. Compensation shall be paid in cash in principle, but when compensation in cash is disadvantageous to the State, compensation in kind may be allowed;
  2. The amount of compensation shall be assessed on the basis of the current value of the relevant commodity at the time the loss of or damage to the commodity occurred, and where the time such fact occurred is unclear, the amount of compensation shall be assessed on the basis of the current value at the time such fact was discovered; 
  3. The current value of a lost or damaged commodity shall be assessed after a close investigation into the price, degree of depreciation, service life, quantity, etc. of the relevant commodity at the time the fact of the loss or damage occurred or such fact was discovered.

Article 3 (Written Order of Compensation Prior to Determination by the Board of Audit and Inspection) The written order of compensation under Article 6 (1) and (2) of the Act shall be as in the attached Form.
  [This Article Newly Inserted by Presidential Decree No. 29304, Nov. 27, 2018]

